{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>And they grew hot.</b> They conceived. This word is unusual in its pointing because of the guttural letter, and it ought to have been like וישבו לאכל לחם (Genesis 37:25). Do not wonder that he used the language of וכרים for the flock, for the way of the language is to distinguish between males and females in the singular, but in the plural they do not distinguish:" "<b>Unto the rods.</b> From the rods. And many will wonder, and they will say that this is a marvel, and it is true that it is among the marvels of nature, and so too the matter even of the woman who was created in the image of the angels:" "<b>And streaked.</b> They are the speckled, for it is a general term:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:29.573242938Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}